.TH SCRIBE 1 "2026-05-04" "scribe 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scribe \- binary forensics, SBOM, security pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scribe
.RI [ global-options ]
.I subcommand
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B scribe
is a Zig\-native binary forensics library and CLI. It parses ELF, Mach\-O, PE,
WebAssembly, and AR archive formats with zero\-copy techniques; extracts
dynamic dependencies, exported and imported symbols, and DWARF function
tables; computes per\-section Shannon entropy and SHA\-256 hashes;
fingerprints functions for static\-library identification; and produces
CycloneDX 1.5 Software Bills of Materials for binaries and full container
images (including direct OCI registry pulls).
.PP
The security pipeline layers in SIMD secret scanning, CVE/advisory
matching, IaC misconfiguration audit, exploit\-mitigation analysis, YARA\-subset
rule matching, and anti\-tampering anomaly detection. Findings flow into a
single CycloneDX SBOM or, for CI, into SARIF 2.1.0 or GitHub Annotations.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-V, version
Print scribe version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help, \-h, help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet, \-q
Suppress the inline progress reporter.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Force\-disable ANSI styling regardless of TTY detection.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Forensics
.TP
.B info \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json] \fR[\-\-all\-slices] \fR[\-\-hashes]
Format, arch, entry point, sections, hardening posture. \-\-all\-slices dumps every slice of a FAT/Universal Mach\-O. \-\-hashes adds per\-section SHA\-256 (first 8 bytes hex).
.TP
.B harden \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Cross\-format exploit\-mitigation report (PIE, NX, RELRO, CFG, GS, code\-sig, ...).
.TP
.B yara \fIpath\fR \-\-rules \fIp\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Match a YARA\-subset rule file against the target.
.TP
.B hex \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-offset 0x...] \fR[\-\-length N] \fR[\-\-section name]
Hex + ASCII dump.
.TP
.B exports \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Dynamically\-exported symbols.
.TP
.B imports \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Dynamically\-imported symbols.
.TP
.B diff \fIa\fR \fIb\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Structural diff: format, arch, sections, hardening posture.
.TP
.B deps \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Dynamic library dependencies.
.TP
.B strings \fIpath\fR \fR[min] \fR[\-\-json]
SIMD\-accelerated printable\-ASCII run extractor.
.TP
.B entropy \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
Shannon entropy per section.
.TP
.B wasm \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
List WebAssembly module sections.
.TP
.B ar list \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json]
List members of a static archive (.a / .lib).
.TP
.B sbom \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-plain]
CycloneDX 1.5 SBOM. Source: file path, docker save tar, docker:// URI, or registry:// URI.
.TP
.B symbols \fIpath\fR
DWARF function table (ELF or Mach\-O dSYM).
.TP
.B addr2line \fIpath\fR \fIhex-addr\fR
Resolve runtime address to source file:line:column.
.TP
.B fp generate|match
Function\-byte fingerprint database (Wyhash, DWARF\-keyed). \fBgenerate\fR writes JSON corpus; \fBmatch\fR runs corpus against a target.
.SS Security pipeline
.TP
.B secrets \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-json] \fR[\-\-include\-generic] \fR[\-\-include\-wide] \fR[\-\-min\-entropy N]
SIMD anchored + UTF\-16LE secret scan with optional entropy filter.
.TP
.B vulns \fIpath\fR \-\-db \fIp\fR \fR[\-\-json]
CVE / advisory matcher (binary, container tar, or OCI registry source).
.TP
.B config \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-type dockerfile|kubernetes] \fR[\-\-json]
IaC misconfiguration audit.
.TP
.B scan \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-db p] \fR[\-\-config p] \fR[\-\-fp\-db p] \fR[\-\-yara p] \fR[\-\-include\-generic] \fR[\-\-include\-wide] \fR[\-\-plain] \fR[\-\-sarif] \fR[\-\-github\-annotations]
Full pipeline: SBOM + secrets + vulns + IaC + fingerprints + hardening + anomalies + YARA. Output is CycloneDX 1.5 by default; \-\-plain for human\-readable; \-\-sarif for SARIF 2.1.0; \-\-github\-annotations for GitHub Actions workflow commands.
.TP
.B policy \fIpath\fR \-\-policy \fIp\fR \fR[\-\-db d] \fR[\-\-config c] \fR[\-\-json]
Evaluate scan results against a JSON policy. Exits 1 on violation.
.TP
.B vulndb compile|merge|update
Advisory DB management (mmap\-friendly binary .scvd format).
.SS Interactive
.TP
.B ui \fIpath\fR \fR[\-\-db p] \fR[\-\-config p] \fR[\-\-fp\-db p] \fR[\-\-include\-generic] \fR[\-\-include\-wide]
Open libvaxis TUI over the same pipeline as \fBscan\fR. Tabs for All / Components / Secrets / Vulns / Config / Hardening, search, multi\-select, bookmarks, clipboard yank, export\-diff. Press ? for in\-app key map.
.SS Misc
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Emit shell completion script.
.SH SOURCES
.TP
.B File path
Single binary or docker save tarball.
.TP
.B docker://image[:tag]
Local docker daemon image (spawns docker save under the hood).
.TP
.B registry://[host/]name:tag[@os/arch]
Direct OCI V2 pull over HTTPS, no daemon required.
.SH OUTPUT
Structured output goes to stdout; errors and progress to stderr.
Long\-running operations emit an inline ANSI spinner on stderr when
attached to a TTY; piped/scripted invocations stay byte\-identical.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .scribe-bookmarks.md
Written by the TUI when you press \fBe\fR; subsequent exports diff against this file.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set non\-empty, disables ANSI styling (same effect as \-\-no\-color).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
success
.TP
.B 1
parse error, missing argument, or scan/policy violation
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR file (1),
.BR otool (1),
.BR readelf (1),
.BR dumpbin (1),
.BR yara (1),
.BR codesign (1)
.SH BUGS
Report at the project's GitHub issue tracker.
.SH AUTHOR
scribe contributors.
